From 6083a293c90d54a43b16b90f97e0e55e3ddccd59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Matuszewski <xanewok@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:07:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] llama : fold the MTP catch-up K/V into the target decode
 (LLAMA_MTP_FOLD_C)

The MTP draft's catch-up decode after each target decode only stores the
draft block's K/V for the batch rows; its outputs are never read. With
llama_mtp_fold_init(ctx_tgt, ctx_dft) and llama_mtp_fold_arm(), the next
target decode appends exactly those nodes (graph_mtp up to the cache write)
to its own graph and writes the draft cache, so the speculative driver can
skip the separate decode (llama_mtp_fold_n_last).

Opt-in with LLAMA_MTP_FOLD_C=1; one sequence, one MTP head, separate MTP
cache, single-ubatch token batches up to 64 tokens. Anything else keeps the
catch-up decode. Default behaviour is unchanged.
